{
  "mn42:0.1": "Middle Discourses 42 ",
  "mn42:0.2": "The People of Verañjā ",
  "mn42:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn42:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn42:2.1": "Now at that time the brahmins and householders of Verañjā were residing in Sāvatthī on some business. ",
  "mn42:2.2": "The brahmins and householders of Verañjā heard: ",
  "mn42:2.3": "“It seems the ascetic Gotama—a Sakyan, gone forth from a Sakyan family—is staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn42:2.4": "He has this good reputation … ",
  "mn42:2.5": "",
  "mn42:2.6": "",
  "mn42:2.7": "",
  "mn42:2.8": "It’s good to see such perfected ones.” ",
  "mn42:3.1": "… They said to the Buddha: ",
  "mn42:4.1": "“What is the cause, worthy Gotama, what is the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after death, are reborn in a place of loss, a bad place, the underworld, hell? ",
  "mn42:4.2": "And what is the cause, worthy Gotama, what is the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after death, are reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm?” ",
  "mn42:5.1": "“Unprincipled and immoral conduct is the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after death, are reborn in a place of loss, a bad place, the underworld, hell. ",
  "mn42:5.2": "Principled and moral conduct is the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after deat